usage: writ diff <old.json> <new.json> <events.jsonl> [--json]

Replay recorded events (one JSON object per line) under both policies and print each event
whose verdict changed, state_version aside, then a count, noting the events both policies
rejected. The file holds one session: it starts with a session_start and holds no other.
Each policy may be layer 1 or 2. Each run starts from a fresh state under its own policy
digest, and diff sets every event's state_version, and a session_start's policy_digest
(which may be left out), to that run's, so one changed verdict does not turn every later
event into a mismatch.
  --json   print one JSON object per changed event instead, and no count

Exit 0 when no verdict changed, 1 when one did, 2 for a usage, IO or policy error, an event
line that is empty or does not parse or decode, or a file that does not start with a
session_start or holds a second one.
